        "created_at": "2015-02-15T00:44:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The question has an official answer, even if it was from playtesting.</p><p>The original donstructs were worded that when they were dealt damage or destroyd their effect happened, and then it was changed to the current wording.</p><p>I specifically asked ifthat changed how they worked when damage would destroy them, and Christopher answered that they did change, that when reduced to 0 hp or less they would not trigger because they would leave play first.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Playing it differently isn't some horrible crime, it just isn't the official way. &nbsp;It does create one infinite loop, but it is a rare and difficult one.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:06:49.091Z",
